  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Kernite <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Na</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>4</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math></p><p>The chemical formula for Kernite is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Na</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>4</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>. It contains boron.</p><p>Cassiterite <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>SnO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p>Cassiterite is an ore of&nbsp;Sn.It &nbsp;is&nbsp;also called&nbsp;tinstone and has molecular formula of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>SnO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>â€‹.</p><p>Calamine <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ZnCO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></p><p>Calamine is an ore of&nbsp;zinc.&nbsp;It is zinc carbonate&nbsp;ZnCO<sub>3</sub>â€‹.</p><p>Cryolite <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Na</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>AlF</mi><mn>6</mn></msub></math>, which consists of Aluminium, Sodium &amp; Fluorine.</p>"
